// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6581 Add AD CS / ESC coverage-gap detections (14 rules)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6581
// Pull request author: elhoim
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious ADCS CA Configuration Weakened Via Certutil.EXE
// Sigma ID: 32a1966a-c4cb-4d86-a667-365256a1be60
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: elhoim
// Date: 2026-10-15 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, credential-access, defense-impairment, T1649
// Description: Detects the use of "certutil.exe -setreg" to apply an insecure configuration to an Active
//   Directory Certificate Services (ADCS) Certification Authority: - Enabling the
//   "EDITF_ATTRIBUTESUBJECTALTNAME2" policy flag, which allows any requester to specify an arbitrary
//   Subject Alternative Name (ESC6). - Removing the "IF_ENFORCEENCRYPTICERTREQUEST" interface flag,
//   which allows unencrypted ICertPassage RPC enrollment and NTLM relay to the CA (ESC11). - Adding
//   the szOID_NTDS_CA_SECURITY_EXT OID (1.3.6.1.4.1.311.25.2) to "DisableExtensionList", which
//   globally removes the SID security extension from issued certificates (ESC16).
// False positives:
//   - Administrators intentionally applying these settings, which is strongly discouraged
// References:
//   - https://www.specterops.io/assets/resources/Certified_Pre-Owned.pdf
//   - https://github.com/ly4k/Certipy/wiki/06-%E2%80%90-Privilege-Escalation
//   - https://blog.compass-security.com/2022/11/relaying-to-ad-certificate-services-over-rpc/
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/certutil
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/f669b19474f70bf0caf3142411b7509cf48c96b5/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_certutil_adcs_insecure_ca_config.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\certutil.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "CertUtil.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-setreg" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/setreg" or ProcessCommandLine contains "–setreg" or ProcessCommandLine contains "—setreg" or ProcessCommandLine contains "―setreg") and (((ProcessCommandLine contains "+EDITF_ATTRIBUTESUBJECTALTNAME2" or ProcessCommandLine contains " EDITF_ATTRIBUTESUBJECTALTNAME2") or ProcessCommandLine contains "-IF_ENFORCEENCRYPTICERTREQUEST") or ((ProcessCommandLine contains "DisableExtensionList" and ProcessCommandLine contains "1.3.6.1.4.1.311.25.2") and (not(ProcessCommandLine contains "-1.3.6.1.4.1.311.25.2"))))
